@startuml SABER Task Framework Architecture - Detailed

!theme plain
title SABER Task Framework - Detailed Architecture

skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor lightblue
    BorderColor black
    ArrowColor black
    FontSize 10
}

package "Task Framework Core" {

    class TaskManager {
        +domain: str
        +tasks: Dict[str, Task]
        +config_loader: TaskConfigLoader
        +episode_manager: EpisodeManager
        --
        +get_task(task_id): Task
        +get_subtask(task_id, subtask_id): SubTask
        +start_episode(session_id, task_id): Episode
        +get_current_episode(session_id): Episode?
        +step(session_id, action, command_result): Step
        +reset(session_id, task_id): Episode
        +end_episode(session_id, reason): Episode
        +reset_episode(session_id): Episode
        +list_tasks(): List[Dict]
        +get_episode_info(session_id): Dict
    }

    class TaskConfigLoader {
        +domain: str
        --
        +load_tasks_from_file(): Dict[str, Task]
        +_parse_task(): Task
        +_parse_subtask(): SubTask
    }

    class Task {
        +task_id: str
        +domain: str
        +title: str
        +description: str
        +subtasks: List[SubTask]
        +initial_context: Dict[str, Any]
        --
        +add_subtask(): void
        +get_subtask_by_id(): SubTask?
        +is_complete(): bool
        +get_all_subtask_ids(): Set[str]
    }

    class SubTask {
        +subtask_id: str
        +task_id: str
        +title: str
        +description: str
        +objective: str
        --
        +is_dependent_on(): bool
    }
}

package "Episode Management" {

    class EpisodeManager {
        +active_episodes: Dict[str, Episode]
        --
        +start_episode(session_id, task_id, initial_context?): Episode
        +step(session_id, action, command_result): Step
        +end_episode(session_id, reason): Episode
        +reset_episode(session_id, task_id): Episode
        +get_episode_state(session_id): EpisodeState?
        +get_current_episode(session_id): Episode?
        +create_step(episode, action, response): Step
        +update_episode_state(episode, step): void
        +cleanup_session(session_id): void
    }

    class Episode {
        +episode_id: str
        +task_id: str
        +session_id: str
        +start_time: datetime
        +end_time: Optional[datetime]
        +state: EpisodeState
        +steps: List[Step]
        +context: Dict[str, Any]
        +metadata: Dict[str, Any]
        +completion_reason: Optional[str]
        --
        +add_step(): void
        +get_executed_commands(): List[str]
        +is_complete: bool (property)
        +duration: Optional[float] (property)
    }

    class Step {
        +step_number: int
        +timestamp: datetime
        +action: Action
        +response: Dict[str, Any]
        +context_snapshot: Dict[str, Any]
        +done: bool
    }

    class Action {
        +tool_name: str
        +parameters: Dict[str, Any]
        +timestamp: datetime
        +command: Optional[str]
    }

    enum EpisodeState {
        CREATED
        ACTIVE
        COMPLETED
        FAILED
        TIMEOUT
        RESET
    }
}

' Relationships
TaskManager *-- TaskConfigLoader
TaskManager *-- EpisodeManager
TaskManager *-- Task

TaskConfigLoader ..> Task : creates
TaskConfigLoader ..> SubTask : creates

Task *-- SubTask

EpisodeManager *-- Episode
Episode *-- Step
Step *-- Action
Episode ..> EpisodeState

note top of TaskManager
**Task Orchestrator**
Coordinates task loading, episode management, and RL interfaces.
Simplified to focus on coordination between specialized components.
Provides gym-style step() and reset() methods for RL compatibility.
Subtasks are retained for informational purposes only.
end note

note top of Task
**Simplified Task Definition**
Tasks contain basic task information and subtasks for reference.
No progression logic, dependency validation, or state tracking.
Subtasks are purely informational elements returned at episode start.
end note

note top of EpisodeManager
**Episode Lifecycle Manager**
Manages RL-style episodes with gym-compatible interfaces.
Returns Step objects directly from step() method.
Handles episode state transitions and completion detection.
Single source of truth for episode operations.
end note

note top of TaskConfigLoader
**YAML Configuration Loader**
Loads and validates task definitions directly from YAML files.
Creates Task and SubTask objects from YAML data structures.
No dependency validation or progression logic.
Single responsibility: YAML parsing and object creation.
end note

note bottom of Episode
**RL Episode State**
Contains complete action-response history for RL training.
No subtask progression tracking or state management.
Provides properties for current state access.
Includes completion information and metadata.
end note

@enduml
